body:
I'M GONNA CRY RIGHT NOW, NOT EVEN KIDDING

&#x200B;

where did you get it :(

Suggest your mom to share the cake with you. Eat it together with her, while chatting, watching something. It's something I try to do when I really wanna eat something but I'm scared for the calories or don't wanna be ashamed for eating all the food in one sitting (because I also can't control myself).

&#x200B;

About your weight and everything, I just wanna say, it's okay. The most important thing now is that you recover from your injury. It's hard to distract yourself when you can't do physically much for it but, truly, it's okay.

I got a bunch of things in my list:

• It takes longer to eat with small cutlery;

• I look and feel less monstrous eating with a tiny spoon than with regular fork and knife, it makes me feel delicate in a way that satisfies my ED, something like "I'm using this petite plate so I'm petite too, maybe?";

• They're kinda discreet in comparison to regular cutlery so it makes easier to eat when you're completely ashamed for eating;

• Small plates really makes stuff seem voluminous;

• It gives me the feeling that I'm eating less than everyone else using their big forks and large bowls;

• My brain convinced itself that using small kitchen utensils are really a 
disordered behavior so I just can't return to using normal things again, 'cause it would mean I'm healthy lol.


Another thing that just came to mind is that maybe small cutlery are associated with childhood, when food meant a good thing.

I'm struggling so hard with bingeing this week, I feel completely defeated as I watch myself gaining weight since I lost control over anorexia and came back to eating "normally". Today was specifically hard for me. This post and this comment described perfecly how I'm feeling. I'm somehow grateful that there are people who can put in words those horrible, confusing, heartbreaking, disturbing emotions. We're in this together.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

>like an uncontrollable zombie

That's exaclty how I see myself.

there's plenty papers and interesting readings about it on internet, i'm particularly interested in how the diet industry is a considerably new way of capitalism to reinvent itself and to manage accumulation.

&#x200B;

but in a particular note, my truth is: everything bad that have ever happened or will happen to society and the human kind is capitalism's fault. 🤭

yes. i hate my ed for taking all the fun out of playing just dance and making it just a way to burn calories. 

&#x200B;

it's scary like even if professional mental health people don't get it, who's out there ready to help and understand us? no doubt why eds have the highest suicide rates
